<binaryimage arch="x86:LE:64:default:gcc">
<!--
    A register the callee leaves alone carries a value across the call.

    gcc -O2 allocates registers across a call to a leaf it compiled in the same
    unit (-fipa-ra): it sets an argument register once and hands it to two
    calls of a leaf it knows does not write it, and it keeps a value in a
    killed-by-call register across such a leaf. The convention says nothing
    survives; the leaf's own decoded body says it does.

        reg:   mov rax,rsi ; add rax,[rdi] ; ret
        fill:  mov byte [rdi],0x41 ; ret
        mtf:   mov eax,[rip+0x2fda] ; add eax,edi ; ret

        twice: push rbx ; mov rbx,rdi ; xor esi,esi ; call reg
               lea rdi,[rbx+8] ; mov rbx,rax ; call reg
               add rax,rbx ; pop rbx ; ret

    The second reg call reads the ESI zeroed before the first. Upstream's
    AncestorRealistic takes any register value that crosses a call as
    clobbered, so the second call lost its argument.

        pipe:  push rbx ; mov rbx,rdi ; mov edi,[rdi] ; mov edx,0x40
               mov esi,1 ; call mtf ; mov edi,[rbx+4] ; mov [rbx],eax
               call mtf ; mov [rbx+4],eax ; pop rbx ; ret

    The second mtf call reads the EDX set before the first. x86-64-gcc.cspec
    lists RDX in <killedbycall>, and calleepreserves declined to narrow it:
    mtf stores nothing and writes no preserved register, and its one memory
    read is a direct ram operand, not a LOAD. The second call read an EDX with
    no definition.

    stale is the control: fill also leaves RSI alone but never reads it, so
    the 7 left in ESI is not an argument of the second fill call.

        stale: push rbx ; mov rbx,rdi ; mov esi,7 ; call fill
               lea rdi,[rbx+1] ; call fill ; pop rbx ; ret

    persistcalls_sem_x86_64's snipsys is the return-register control: a
    void function that ends `syscall; jmp f1`, where f1 only increments
    globals. A body that only reads memory keeps argument registers alive,
    not RAX, so the syscall's RAX is not snipsys's return value.

    Stage: P3 heritage call guards and P4 argument recovery
    (kuna_calleepreserves.rs, kuna_calleescratchbody.rs). A strict fix with
    no option.
-->
